# Context Building & Token Budgets

Applies to `src/vs/ai/context/` — context gathering, prioritization, and anything that assembles text to send to an AI provider.

## Token-budgeted `gatherContext()`

Context gathering is bounded by a `MAX_TOKENS` budget: keep adding context (current file, then open files, in priority order) until the next item would exceed the budget, then stop — never gather unbounded context and truncate at the provider call site.

```typescript
export class ContextManager {
    private readonly MAX_TOKENS = 4000;

    async gatherContext(options: ContextOptions = {}): Promise<CodeContext> {
        const currentFile = await this.getCurrentFileContext();
        let tokensUsed = this.estimateTokens(currentFile?.content || '');

        const openFiles: FileContext[] = [];

        for (const file of this.getOpenFiles()) {
            const fileTokens = this.estimateTokens(file.content);
            if (tokensUsed + fileTokens > this.MAX_TOKENS) {
                break;
            }
            openFiles.push(file);
            tokensUsed += fileTokens;
        }

        return { currentFile, openFiles };
    }

    private estimateTokens(text: string): number {
        // Rough estimation: 1 token ≈ 4 characters
        return Math.ceil(text.length / 4);
    }
}
```

- Highest-priority context (current file / active selection) is added first, before opportunistically filling remaining budget with less-critical context (other open files, project structure, git diff).
- The `Math.ceil(text.length / 4)` heuristic is intentionally rough — don't replace it with an expensive real tokenizer call in a hot path (e.g. inline completions) unless profiling shows the cheap estimate is actually causing budget overruns.

## Performance

- **Lazy-load AI components** — don't initialize providers, indexes, or context managers until a feature that needs them is actually invoked.
- **Cache AI responses** where the request is deterministic/repeatable — avoid redundant provider calls for the same context+query.
- **Debounce rapid requests**, especially inline completions triggered on every keystroke — batch/coalesce before hitting a provider.
- **Respect token limits** end-to-end — a context manager that respects `MAX_TOKENS` is undermined if a caller bypasses it and concatenates extra text before sending.

## Privacy & security

- **Never log API keys** — not in console output, error messages, or telemetry.
- **Filter PII before sending to AI providers** — code comments, commit messages, and file contents can carry names/emails/secrets; strip or redact before context leaves the process boundary.
- **Support local-only mode** — context-gathering and provider selection must degrade gracefully when the user has configured a local model and no data should leave the machine.
- **Encrypt sensitive storage** — cached context, conversation history, and API keys at rest use the editor's secret storage, not plain settings files.
